  m_Name: DadRepeated
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NarratorEventData
  eventID: DadRepeated
  dialogueLines:
  - The player has already spoken to their dad. Perhaps they should find something
    else to do.
  - "The player has already seen their dad. There\u2019s no need to bother him again."
  - "The player has checked in with their dad. Maybe it\u2019s time to explore somewhere
    else."
  - The players dad has already been visited. Perhaps the player should move on.
  - The player has already said hello to their dad. There must be something else
    to investigate.
  - "There\u2019s nothing more to see here. Perhaps the player should look around
    the office."
  - The player has already found their dad. Now what else could there be to discover?
  - The players dad is already accounted for. Time to see what else the office has
    to offer.
  - The player has already had their conversation with dad. Perhaps they should leave
    him to work.
  - "Dad has been checked on. Surely there\u2019s something else for the player to
    get up to."
  - "The player has already seen their dad. Perhaps there\u2019s something else to
    do."
  - The player has already checked in with dad. Time to find something else.
  - "There\u2019s nothing new to see with dad. Perhaps the player should move along."
  - The player has already spoken to their dad. Maybe they should explore the rest
    of the office.
  - Dad has already been seen. Surely the player can find something else to occupy
    their time.
  - "The player has already stopped by dad\u2019s desk. Perhaps another desk would
    be more interesting."
  - "Their dad has already been checked on. Maybe it\u2019s time for the player to
    wander elsewhere."
  - The player has already had a look at what dad is doing. There must be something
    else around here.
  - Dad is still busy working. The player has already seen him, so perhaps they should
    leave him to it.
  - The player has already paid dad a visit. Maybe they should see what else is happening.
  - "There\u2019s no reason to keep visiting dad. The office has plenty of other
    things to see."
  - The player has already found their dad. Now perhaps they should find something
    else.
  - Dad has been seen, greeted, and accounted for. Maybe the player should move on.
  - "The player has already checked on dad. Perhaps it\u2019s time to explore somewhere
    new."
  canRepeat: 1
  priority: 3
